  "headline": "DSI To Mandate NADI Portal For Strategic Commodity Exports In 2027",
  "seoTitle": "DSI To Mandate NADI Portal For Strategic Commodity Exports",
  "metaDescription": "Starting January 1, 2027, the DSI will require exports of strategic commodities like coal and palm oil to be processed through the NADI portal system.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The DSI is set to implement a unified export process for strategic commodities, including coal and palm oil, starting January 1, 2027.",
    "The NADI portal will be used to monitor export data and address practices such as under-invoicing to prevent potential revenue losses.",
    "PT PLN (Persero) is simultaneously strengthening its own strategies to secure domestic coal supplies for power generation reliability."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Beginning January 1, 2027, Indonesia plans to streamline the export process for key strategic commodities, such as coal and palm oil, through the DSI-managed NADI portal. This initiative aims to centralize export monitoring and close loopholes, including cases of under-invoicing that may lead to revenue leakage. As part of these broader regulatory changes, the DSI is actively collecting data from exporters and evaluating price index methodologies for commodities. Parallel to these export developments, the state-owned utility company PT PLN (Persero) has announced enhanced strategies to ensure the security and reliability of coal supplies for national power generation. While the industry adjusts to these new reporting requirements, some contractors are shifting focus toward mineral mining diversification, and legal proceedings against individuals involved in past coal financing project disputes are ongoing.",
